{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For there is no divination in Jacob.</b> An expression of testing, like נחשתי — meaning, one should not test whether He will curse them, for He will surely not curse them. And if you ask: the Holy One, blessed be He, does not want to curse them, but through sorceries and spells a person can curse them — therefore it says ולא קסם בישראל, that no sorceries avail against them, for the Holy One, blessed be He, guards them." "<b>According to this time it shall be said of Jacob.</b> The time to come, like כעת חיה. It shall be said of Jacob and of Israel: מה פעל אל — meaning, the Holy One, blessed be He, will perform miracles and mighty acts for Israel to such a degree that everyone will say: How many deeds the Holy One, blessed be He, has wrought with these. And it is like מה רבו מעשיך ה׳."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:04.949581167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}